  "features": [
    "Node observer callbacks return actual exported PerformanceObserverEntryList instances with privately owned chronological buffers and a standard toStringTag.",
    "Public construction and invalid receivers use native error codes; method signatures, missing-argument validation, string coercion and nullish optional type filtering match the control.",
    "Getters return independent arrays without exposing the owned buffer, preserving entry object identities across filtering."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The initial Node signature control expected getEntriesByName.length=2; Node reports 1. The corrected default parameter/control passed and the mistaken control remains without passing credit.",
    "Two intermediate build admissions refused low disk; obsolete task executables/objects were pruned only after terminal builds, newest outputs were preserved, and cache manifests moved aside before rebuilding. Inventories and cleanup summary are retained; cache metadata copies are excluded from evidence.",
    "Full resource timing creation/buffering, supported-type breadth, inspection/global-constructor interactions and remaining performance option/error semantics remain open under #869.",
    "Pickier reports no errors and four existing style warnings in the upstream modules.",
    "Windows measurement, Linux execution, wider startup paths, previous ICU contradiction #872, complete Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership and Release/ASAN/all-platform verification remain open under #66."
  ],
